    "label": "thm: regret_bound",
    "number": "Theorem 3.1",
    "quote": "Suppose that Assumption \\ref{ass: normalization} and \\ref{ass: lipschitz} hold. Then the expected cumulative regret of Algorithm \\ref{alg: general} satisfies the bound\n\\begin{equation}\n    \\begin{aligned}\n    \\nonumber\n        &\\mathbb{E}[\\text{Regret}(T) ] \\leq \n        \\underbrace{2C_1k_1T_0  \\vphantom{\\sum_{t = T_0}^T } }_{(a)} + \n        \\underbrace{ 2C_1 k_1 \\sum_{t = T_0}^T \\left[  \\mathbb{P} \\left( \\mathcal{A}_{T_0}^c \\right) + \\mathbb{P}(\\mathcal{E}_{T_0}^c)\\right]}_{(b)} \\\\\n        & +\\underbrace{ 2C_2 \\sum_{t = T_0}^T \\sqrt{9 \\dfrac{\\lambda_{T_0}^2}{\\alpha^2} \\phi^2 + \\dfrac{1}{\\alpha}[2Z_{T_0}(\\theta^*) + 4 \\lambda_{T_0} R(\\theta^*_{\\mathcal{M}^{\\bot}})]} }_{(c)}"
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Generic framework bound; sums over t from T_0 to T written as (T-T_0+1) times constant summand. Corollary A.1 gives an analogous bound with Assumptions in the regularizer norm R, third term 8C_2 phi sum sqrt(9 lambda^2 phi^2/alpha^2 + 2 lambda Z/alpha) assuming theta* in M."
  },
